I tried calibrating but I noticed the new settings will go away after powering cycle the radio! it only saves while the radio still on.<br><br>I also  could not fix the issue yet as it is a slow and painful process: change the calibration value, hit green to (partially) save it, power cycle the hotspot to start the radio in hotspot mode, wait x minutes to boot, when radio enters hotspot mode, wait for a an active TG to hear the results, than get disappointment that the issue still there <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_smile.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=":)" title="Smile">  start all over Even if I could find the right value, it will go away if I turn the radio off!<br><br>One thing I found, it is certainly hardware related! I got a second 1701, loaded OGD77 in it and this one worked fine in hotspot mode, at least on a quick test. However I need try calibrating the bad 1701 but simply having a extreme hard time to do it.<br><br>I re-loaded OGD77 in it and tried to copy the new 1701 calibration to the bad one but it did not work!<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7412">K4BMI</a> — Wed Jan 15, 2025 4:36 pm</p><hr />
