<blockquote class="uncited"><div>That is correct, when I have the TYTs as modem, all works ok, but the 1701 just garbles and distorts the audio.<br><br>I am familiar with the WPSD config file and will look there however never touched the openGD77 calibration menu before, is there a guide or reference with the steps on how to calibrate using it? The Official guide mentions frequency adjustment but the steps there are just for TX power adjustment.<br><br>I would try adjusting  in the mmdvmhost config file, however I have two other radios, so ideally I would need adjust the 1701 instead.</div></blockquote>You can step down to frequency calibration with SK2+Down Arrow when you are in the calibration menu.<br><br>I have used my frequency counter and adjusted all radios and hotspots to be as accurate as possible.<br>Bit error is less than 0.2% in pi-star nodes.<br><br>You can also use a SDR with VHF/UHF coverage and at least adjust all your equipment to use the same carrier frequency.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Mon Jan 06, 2025 9:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
