		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4733&amp;p=35003#p35003"><![CDATA[
I am not sure if anybody else having this issue but my 1701 just does work well while in Hotspot mode. I tried BlueDV and connect it to a Raspberry PI but audio is distorted and stuttering. <br><br>I tried adjust the BER in both Pi-Star and WPSD but neither will start the adjustment mode. Tried it directly using SSH "sudo pistar-mmdvmcal" and it says board not supported.<br><br>Adding ferrite chocks to the USB cable did nothing. The modulation even starts audible but it breaks up after a few seconds becoming garbled.<br>I know it is something with the 1701 because I tried a TYT9600 and a TYT 390 plus and both wotk fine. Not sure where to go from here.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=7412">K4BMI</a> — Sun Jan 05, 2025 6:04 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
